      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "63664132-d050-5ee8-a33d-be6b5f92be12",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n\n- **III.** The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0775397b-d287-5978-97a3-285fa18a12a9",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "1bed54d0-db4b-5239-a212-639be5a7626b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e5581757-5536-5c90-b01f-6d5717ac30c1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "1bed54d0-db4b-5239-a212-639be5a7626b"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8e0c9c06-3531-5ce5-8c67-00d13114acb2",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "797077d9-f322-5360-b557-9464065ecb7d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3296584d-cb06-5928-baaf-a0fd646a0bef",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "797077d9-f322-5360-b557-9464065ecb7d"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a94a6713-9f50-5edb-9ebc-35c07688e09f",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "4f12457b-b00b-59fb-9967-2cefe400ec3f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "69ebdc7b-8df5-5b11-a589-b5c9bc4485e0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "69ebdc7b-8df5-5b11-a589-b5c9bc4485e0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
