    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9d5158af-8798-5fa3-b64b-673c46cbb9cf",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\csc x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$.\n- **II.** The function has a zero at $x = \\frac{-5π}{2}$.\n- **III.** The function takes the value $-1$ at $x =-\\frac{π}{2} + 2nπ$.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bb4543ee-9ff9-5047-9fa3-40ebe71febb2",
