  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176053,
      "id": "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326",
      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f4a31060-0f63-579a-8b3f-de57acb8fff7",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{-11\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n\n- **III.** The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "254c853d-4ae0-5eaa-b477-3e807a712ac7",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "12c5e4ba-37de-554b-8c4e-8a4e4c015b7c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5ed25953-5145-5099-8b82-95c9884f8c01",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "12c5e4ba-37de-554b-8c4e-8a4e4c015b7c"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a93e0eb9-01a9-53f3-be07-e49c589e1c5f",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "4db85b58-7ce1-54ca-b5e4-7dad044fb9ed",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "a1a211b7-8b99-558d-88ff-09270e9f2bc0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "4db85b58-7ce1-54ca-b5e4-7dad044fb9ed"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0c866620-f099-5b83-b712-a59d40800112",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "c8797dd9-1e52-5c1d-b88d-2d878dddba4c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e2cdb6f5-775c-5a12-bb40-b986016c0a7e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "e2cdb6f5-775c-5a12-bb40-b986016c0a7e"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
