  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176053,
      "id": "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326",
      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "270afce9-c1d4-52aa-982f-ccc0142c2054",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$\n- **III.** $x=12\\pi $ is in the domain of the function.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1a5c7238-5051-5d8d-98cb-2e5ee0bcbba2",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "635214b8-d46c-5fdf-8f2c-721dc06e700b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "aa491fe7-9c29-5c76-8809-afe2b40426e2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "635214b8-d46c-5fdf-8f2c-721dc06e700b"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8fc8e98b-19bb-5b30-ab2b-8d346387b627",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "e1303542-e227-5f98-ba38-4f9e8a3b8212",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "60d50664-52dd-5e37-9d32-e866aed92b0f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "60d50664-52dd-5e37-9d32-e866aed92b0f"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3559829f-7fad-5a70-9f83-f5f9025ef742",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "25533e2e-7ba6-59dc-910b-83b494a8a935",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f6de175b-c75c-5067-84c0-82ea6cc9f557",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "25533e2e-7ba6-59dc-910b-83b494a8a935"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $12\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
