  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176053,
      "id": "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326",
      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cbe095ac-d8db-52aa-a9d6-bf6d0f75774d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{-9\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n\n- **III.** The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3f5cc385-9eec-5598-98e3-bfe404cd1a24",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "65b8faa6-bf01-57cb-89ce-8ab31fe1d1ff",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "93896738-ff1a-5c17-b5db-3656220d1b3c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "65b8faa6-bf01-57cb-89ce-8ab31fe1d1ff"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4edf7875-a4b9-57ac-b3e7-bb1cce8f2187",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "f464680a-8c2c-54b7-89f8-051e0b863e5e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "018602ba-11b6-5d3f-abed-f8b69f96fa77",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f464680a-8c2c-54b7-89f8-051e0b863e5e"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a7869d97-039c-5eae-99c0-70967ba9af5c",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "96ae3738-f4ac-500e-a91b-c6ff620f662a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "cef0d6c3-3e35-5506-bded-2aa190370d4f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "cef0d6c3-3e35-5506-bded-2aa190370d4f"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
    "generation": {
      "version": "cosecant-properties-2-checkbox",
