    "question": {
      ":question/id": "10476bbf-32ee-5740-b81a-5afe061b45b9",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+8\\pi ).$\n- **III.** $x=-13\\pi $ is in the domain of the function.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ce5a59b4-531f-5e5e-9321-ed86db16793e",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "dd809c3d-b2a8-5251-90cd-bd052735a792",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "900eb28e-f4df-5cc1-9720-4f371baf9c5a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "dd809c3d-b2a8-5251-90cd-bd052735a792"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "eb526704-acd9-5c58-b0d1-975b89c771ed",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "07482504-3a77-58a0-86ee-8edea999c537",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "eab8051f-957b-5657-9e25-9ea2d00518a7",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "eab8051f-957b-5657-9e25-9ea2d00518a7"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b20c2c61-48a5-554c-bf45-9b82c1676b05",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6bcb2302-e3dc-5251-9499-4147784375f1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8ac9cb5e-f446-5682-b272-94fc9018b5bc",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "6bcb2302-e3dc-5251-9499-4147784375f1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=4,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+8\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $-13\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
